    "source": "Introduction",
    "page": 3,
    "text": "Introduction To The Program\nBehind The Scenes:\nCommunication & Structure\nThe Work Behind The Artist\nA serious artist carries more responsibility than the audience ever\nsees. Beyond writing, recording, and performing, there is\nplanning, communication, scheduling, promotion, approvals, and\ncoordination.\nUntil a full team is in place, many of these responsibilities remain\nin the artist hands. That does not mean doing everything alone. It\nmeans communication must stay clear, organized, and consistent.\nWhen a show is confirmed, a release date changes, a deal comes\nin, or a collaboration moves forward, the right people need to\nknow early enough to support the work properly.\nNot every detail needs to be shared, but the right information\nmust reach the right people at the right time. Strong\ncommunication prevents confusion, missed deadlines, and lost\nopportunities.\nCommunication Standards\nKeep Updates Organized\nUse clear emails, direct requests, and simple timelines.\nConfirm Important Details\nFor major opportunities, confirm receipt and follow up in writing.\nRespect Timing\nLate information can affect press, visuals, release planning, and\ndelivery quality.\nProtect Momentum\nClear communication keeps projects moving and allows the team to\nsupport you properly.\nAccelerator Program\nPage 3"
