    "text": "Introduction To The Program\nYour Job As A Rising Artist\nBuild The Connection Between Your Vision And Your\nAudience\nYour role as a rising artist is to take your creative vision and\nconnect it with the right audience. This happens through strong\nmusic, consistent communication, reliable execution, and a clear\nunderstanding of how your work is being presented.\nYou are not expected to know everything. You do not need to\nbecome a lawyer, accountant, manager, promoter, designer,\nproducer, and strategist all at once. Those areas can be\nsupported by professionals as your career grows.\nYour core responsibility is to keep developing the parts only you\ncan lead: your sound, your story, your performance, your\nmessage, your consistency, and your relationship with your\naudience.\nMusic is not only about being heard. It is about making people feel\nsomething and giving them a reason to keep paying attention. The\nartists who grow are the ones who stay committed, communicate\nclearly, and keep showing up.\nArtist Responsibilities\nCreate Strong Music\nFocus on quality, identity, and emotional connection.\nStay Consistent\nGrowth depends on repeated effort, not isolated moments.\nCommunicate Clearly\nSupport works best when the artist gives clear direction and timely\nupdates.\nKeep The Show Going\nChallenges will happen. Professional artists continue building\nthrough them.\nAccelerator Program\nPage 4"
