    "source": "Branding",
    "page": 4,
    "text": "Accelerator Program\nBranding 101\nPage 4\nBranding 101\nExercises For Artists\nDefining Identity, Audience & Brand Direction\nUse the following exercises to clarify your brand identity, understand how your audience sees you,\nand shape the visual and strategic direction of your artist project.\n1. Personal Brand Statement\nComplete the prompt: “I like [Artist Name]\nbecause …” Identify the qualities, values, and\npersonality traits that make your artistic identity\ndistinct.\n2. Audience Perception Exercise\nAsk listeners, supporters, or followers why they\nconnect with your music or content. Their\nanswers will help you understand which parts of\nyour brand are already resonating.\n3. Artistic Manifesto\nComplete the prompt: “I stand for … through my\nart.” Define the values, ideas, or emotions your\nwork represents and the impact you want it to\nhave.\n4. Brand Archetype Exploration\nResearch brand archetypes such as The Rebel,\nThe Creator, or The Lover. Identify which\narchetype best aligns with your artistic persona\nand how it should shape your visuals and\nmessaging.\n5. Visual Branding Mood Board\nCreate a mood board using images, colors,\ntypography, styling references, and design cues\nthat reflect the atmosphere and identity you want\nyour audience to associate with you.\n6. Audience Building\nAsk yourself: Who do I want to reach? Who do I\nimagine attending my shows? Who is engaging\nwith my work today, and how are they\ndiscovering it? These questions help shape a\nmore intentional brand strategy."
