    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 3\nThe Power Of Your Network\nThe Power Of Asking\nQuestions Open Doors\nNo artist is expected to know everything. The artists who grow fastest are usually not the ones\npretending to have every answer. They are the ones willing to ask, learn, clarify, and start\nconversations.\nAsking can create opportunity. A well-timed message to a director, executive, manager, producer, A&R;,\npublisher, or collaborator can lead to a conversation that would not have happened otherwise. The\nanswer may be no, but no is still better than never entering the room.\nAsking is not only about opportunities. It is also about clarity. If a term, deal point, timeline, or\nexpectation is unclear, ask. A brief moment of discomfort is better than a major mistake later. Strong\nquestions show seriousness, not weakness.\nAsk For Opportunity\nIf the idea is clear and respectful, make the request. Doors do not open for people who never knock.\nAsk For Clarity\nWhen language, contracts, timelines, or expectations are unclear, ask before acting.\nAsk With Respect\nThe goal is not to pressure people. The goal is to start a serious, useful conversation.\nRespect The Person Asking You\nWhen someone asks you for guidance, remember that curiosity is a vulnerable position. Treat it\nprofessionally."
