    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 4\nThe Power Of Your Network\nThe Power Of Communication\nYour Voice Matters\nCommunication is not only digital. In an industry crowded with emails, links, and generic direct\nmessages, a real voice can create stronger connection and clearer understanding. A phone call,\nvoicemail, or personalized voice message can carry tone, urgency, respect, and intent in a way written\ntext often cannot.\nThis does not mean every conversation needs to become a call. It means artists should understand\nwhen a message is too important, too emotional, or too easily misunderstood to be handled casually.\nWhen the moment matters, use the format that gives the conversation the best chance to land correctly.\nCommunication also means refusing to let the past become a cage. Past models, old industry habits,\nand traditional expectations can be useful references, but they are not laws. The artist must know the\ndifference between learning from precedent and being controlled by it.\nUse Your Voice\nAsk for the call when needed. Show up when the\nconversation matters. Send a voice message when it\ncreates a stronger personal connection.\nAvoid Generic Outreach\nA personalized message to a fan, collaborator, or\nindustry contact is stronger than a copied pitch.\nReduce Misinterpretation\nUse calls or voice notes when tone, detail, or urgency\ncould be lost in writing.\nRespect The Past, But Do Not Obey It\nUse the past as reference, not restriction. Strategy\nshould come from the present opportunity, not fear."
