    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 5\nThe Power Of Your Network\nWho Knows You\nNetwork Leverage Is Career Leverage\nNetworking is not collecting business cards, adding people on LinkedIn, or commenting on posts. Real\nnetworking is the process of building meaningful professional relationships that can move a career\nforward. In entertainment, the question is not only who you know. The sharper question is: who knows\nyou?\nA strong network can shorten the path between talent and opportunity. A connected manager, lawyer,\nproducer, publisher, publicist, or executive can save years of guessing by putting the artist closer to\nrooms, decisions, and relationships that matter.\nMajor careers are often built through a combination of talent, timing, strategy, and relationships. Jay-Z,\nTaylor Swift, and Lana Del Rey all benefited from important creative or business relationships that\nhelped shape access, development, or visibility. The lesson is not to copy their path. The lesson is to\nrecognize that relationships compound.\nNetwork With Intention\nKnow what type of relationship you are trying to build before reaching out.\nBe Known For Something\nPeople remember clarity. Make it easy for others to understand your sound, value, goals, and\nprofessionalism.\nRelationships Compound\nOne strong relationship can lead to a collaboration, introduction, placement, booking, or strategic\nopportunity.\nThe Manager Effect\nA well-connected and respected manager can expand an artist network faster than cold outreach alone."
