    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 6\nThe Power Of Your Network\nCareful, Respectful & Assertive\nProfessional Networking Rules\nNetworking is a two-way bridge. Some people will have more recognition, leverage, or access than\nothers. Those people are often careful about new relationships because time, reputation, and trust carry\nreal value in this industry.\nApproach people with respect. Do not downgrade established individuals, overstate your position, or act\nentitled to their access. The strongest networking often begins with genuine interest, mutual respect,\nand a clear reason to connect.\nA relationship built only on what someone can do for you will usually feel transactional. A relationship\nbuilt on respect, shared interests, value, and follow-through has a better chance of lasting.\n1. Identify Your Goals\nDecide whether you are looking for mentors,\ncollaborators, industry contacts, bookings, press,\ncreative partners, or new opportunities.\n2. Research Contacts\nStudy the person, company, position, background, and\nlikely relevance before reaching out.\n3. Reach Out Clearly\nSend a personalized message that explains why you\nare connecting and what makes the conversation\nrelevant.\n4. Engage Properly\nAsk thoughtful questions, listen actively, and avoid\nmaking the exchange feel like a one-sided ask.\n5. Follow Up\nSend a clear thank-you message, continue the\nconversation, and keep the relationship warm.\n6. Give Back\nShare useful resources, make introductions, offer\nsupport, or create value where possible.\n7. Reflect & Improve\nAfter each networking effort, review what worked, what\ndid not, and how to approach better next time.\n8. Stay Professional\nBe assertive without becoming aggressive. Respect\nboundaries, timing, and context."
