    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 8\nThe Power Of Your Network\nYour Industry Contact Map\nAdditional Roles To Track\nA&R;\nA&R; professionals scout, develop, and connect talent\nto labels or music companies. Approach with\ndiscernment. Some are valuable allies. Others may not\nprioritize the artist interest.\nPublicists\nPublicists manage press, public image, interviews,\nreleases, media communication, and reputation\nstrategy.\nMusic Publishers\nPublishers represent compositions, pursue sync\nplacements, collect publishing income, negotiate\nlicensing, and help expand commercial opportunities for\nsongs.\nAgents & Bookers\nAgents and bookers secure live performance\nopportunities, negotiate fees, manage booking logistics,\nand connect artists to venues, brands, festivals, and\nevents.\nRecord Producers\nProducers shape recordings, arrangements, sound,\ndirection, and creative execution. They can also\nbecome important network bridges.\nSound Engineers\nEngineers can become long-term creative partners,\nstudio connectors, producers, or label founders. Build\ntrust with one, but connect with many.\nSongwriters\nSongwriters expand creative reach and often bring their\nown networks. Strong songwriting relationships can\ncreate career momentum and better songs.\nC-Level Executives\nCEOs, CFOs, COOs, CMOs, and senior\ndecision-makers can open major gates. They are hard\nto access directly, which is why managers and lawyers\noften matter."
