    "text": "Accelerator Program\nThe Power Of Your Network\nPage 9\nThe Power Of Your Network\nNetwork Mapping Exercise\nFind The Gaps Before You Need The Door\nThis exercise helps you understand the strength, diversity, and usefulness of your current network. The\ngoal is not to pretend every contact is valuable. The goal is to see where you already have support and\nwhere you are missing access.\n1. Identify Your Network\nList the people you regularly interact with across personal and professional circles, including colleagues,\nfriends, mentors, clients, collaborators, and acquaintances.\n2. Note Name, Status & Occupation\nNext to each person, write their role, field, status, or area of expertise.\n3. Rate The Relationship\nGive each relationship a score from 1 to 10 based on trust, access, communication, and mutual support.\n4. Reflect On The Gaps\nReview which categories are missing. Do you know lawyers, publicists, producers, engineers, publishers,\nbookers, managers, or songwriters?\n5. Set Goals\nChoose specific relationships to strengthen, reconnect with, or build over the next month.\nPerson\nOccupation / Role\nRelationship Score\nNext Action\n/ 10\n/ 10\n/ 10\n/ 10\n/ 10\n/ 10\n/ 10\nOnce the list is built, group your contacts by occupation and identify the missing classes. The next\nchapter can focus on building new communities, including fans. For now, the assignment is simple:\nknow where the gaps are."
