    "text": "The Power Of A Three-Year Plan\nExercise For The Week\nFill out your three-year calendar with all potential opportunities for releases, High Peak\nEvents, videos, marketing pushes, and major business moves. Start broad. Then send\nus a copy so we can help review the structure.\nFinal Reminder\nYou do not need to know the exact venue, brand, sync partner, or festival today. You\nneed a layout that helps you recognize where opportunities belong when they appear.\nThe plan gives the chaos a place to land.\n1. Create\nSet up Year 1, Year 2, and Year 3 in one visible planner.\n2. Add\nReleases\nPlace singles, EPs, albums, remixes, features, and possible release\nwindows.\n3. Add Visuals\nPlace music videos, visualizers, photoshoots, EPK updates, and short-form\ncampaigns.\n4. Add HPEs\nMark festivals, interviews, showcases, sync targets, brand moments, and\nviral opportunities.\n5. Work\nBackward\nAdd rehearsal, production, editing, legal, budget, and outreach deadlines\nbefore each event.\n6. Review\nGaps\nLook for empty months, overpacked months, missing assets, missing\npartners, and moments with no follow-up.\nAccelerator Program\nPage 12\nThe Power Of A Three-Year Plan"
