    "text": "High Peak & Landmark Events\nExercise For The Week\nIntegrate landmark events into your three-year calendar. Do not only write releases. Add events\nthat can create awareness, authority, press, content, collaborators, local support, and business\nmomentum.\nEvery small gig, festival, TV appearance, feature, media moment, sync opportunity, or business\ncollaboration can become a stepping stone when it is prepared, documented, and followed by a\nclear next move.\n1. List Potential Events\nWrite down festivals, venues, shows, media outlets, podcasts, features, sync targets, local\nbusiness ideas, showcases, and online moments that could support your career.\n2. Place Them On The Calendar\nAdd them to your three-year planner by month. Include deadlines for pitching, applications,\nrehearsals, assets, travel, marketing, and content capture.\n3. Choose The Best Targets\nPrioritize events with the strongest audience fit, authority value, and realistic access.\n4. Send The Plan\nPrepare a draft calendar and share it for review so the strategy can become practical instead\nof theoretical.\nAccelerator Program\nHigh Peak & Landmark Events\nPage 12"
