    "source": "Are You Worth Following?",
    "page": 3,
    "text": "Accelerator Program\nAre You Worth Following?\nPage 3\nAre You Worth Following?\nIs It Your Look / Brand Image?\nYour identity and look as an artist are pivotal. Whether you project mystery, authenticity, striking\nvisuals, or a clear sense of style, your appearance can create a profound first impression.\nHowever, while an intentional image can attract people at first, the substance beneath it\ndetermines long-term loyalty. This chapter focuses on the first part of that process: visual\ninterest, artist presence, and whether your image gives people a reason to care.\nAre you putting enough effort into curating your appearance? Are people genuinely drawn to\nyour aesthetics? And by people, we mean unbiased strangers who may think:\nKeep This Line In Mind\n\"Hey, your stuff looks cool. You look interesting. I would want to be your friend and give you a\nfollow.\"\nThis does not mean dyeing your hair pink and calling it a strategy. It does not mean wearing\nrandom attention-seeking clothes with no connection to the music. The real question is sharper:\nare you doing everything possible to express your artist persona at its strongest?\nIf you are serious about this industry, you are not only releasing songs. Music, art, fashion,\nentertainment, content, and show business all connect. Your image is part of the audience\njourney."
