    "source": "Are You Worth Following?",
    "page": 6,
    "text": "Accelerator Program\nAre You Worth Following?\nPage 6\nAre You Worth Following?\nThe Modern Attention Era\nWe are now in an engagement-driven society. In earlier eras, encountering an artist required\neffort: attending shows, joining fan clubs, buying magazines, waiting for radio appearances, or\ngoing to events. Today, the audience expects constant access, instant signals, and fast\nemotional reasons to pay attention.\nThis does not mean you should chase every trend. It means your image, presentation, and\ncontent must give people something to recognize. If an artist lacks engagement or a clear visual\nidentity, they risk falling behind in modern entertainment.\nArtists also increasingly collaborate with brands. These partnerships shape consumer behavior\nand create a sense of belonging around style, identity, and culture. From punk fashion to\nmodern brand collaborations, artists often become symbols that audiences use to express who\nthey are.\nThe point is simple: your visual identity should not be random. It should create excitement,\ninterest, genuine affection, and a reason for people to connect.\nFans Follow Identity\nPeople do not only follow music. They follow a feeling, a world, a style, a signal, and a story they\nwant to be close to."
