    "source": "Social Media Optimization",
    "page": 2,
    "text": "Social Media Optimization\nCatching Up On The Program\nWhy social media optimization comes before fan acquisition\nBefore we go deeper into audience and fan acquisition, we need to make sure your social media\npages are ready to receive people. A new listener may discover you through a song, a story, a\nrecommendation, a show, a reel, or a random profile visit. If your page does not communicate\nwho you are clearly, that attention can disappear in seconds.\nThis chapter focuses mostly on Instagram because it remains one of the fastest places for\npeople to judge your artist image, releases, profile photo, content quality, and credibility. The\ngoal is simple: make your account attractive, clear, organized, and worth following.\nCore Idea\nSocial media is not only a posting tool. Itis a public storefront for your artist identity. Before asking people to\ncare, make sure the page gives them a reason to stay.\nYour account does not need to look like a major label campaign overnight. But it must feel\nintentional. A rising artist can lose attention by looking random, outdated, unclear, or\ninconsistent."
