    "source": "Social Media Optimization",
    "page": 4,
    "text": "Social Media Optimization\nBio Guidelines\nLess information, more direction\nKeep It Simple\nLimit the bio to essential information. Less is usua\nstronger when the rest of the profile already tells the video, tour, or campaign. Give visitors a clear reason\nstory.\nShowcase Content\nFeature links to your latest music, videos, merch,\ntickets, or other creative work. Let the content do\nheavy lifting.\nInvite Curiosity\nThe bio should create interest and movement, not\noverwhelm visitors with credentials.\nHighlight Releases\nlly Use the bio to announce a current single, project,\nto click.\nReflect Your Brand\nUse language that feels like your artist persona.\nthe Avoid unnecessary titles when possible.\nThink of the bio as a first conversation. If someone talks too much, gives too many unrelated\ndetails, and never makes you curious, you may not want a second conversation. Your bio should\nnot feel like that.\nSimple examples can be release driven: latest release out now, new video out now, tour tickets\navailable, or a line that ties directly to the current era of the artist.\ndojacat © EEEID essooe\n@5posts 24M folowers 466 following\nDojacat\nGoowa\no\nwnidojacat.comtour +2"
