    "text": "Social Media Optimization\nBio Examples\nCurrent campaign first, unnecessary labels last\nThe examples below show why the bio does not need to explain every role. It can simply point\npeople toward the current moment: a song, a video, a tour, or an album.\nOlivia Rodrigo Tate McRae\nA lyric-driven bio tied directly to the current release Short, current, and centered around the song that\nand video. needs attention.\nRina Sawayama Conan Gray\nAlbum-forward and visually clean. Project title, mood, and link. Simple enough to\nunderstand fast.\nGriff Billie Eilish\nTour and new music in a direct call-to-action format. A strong example of turning even small bio updates\ninto fan behavior and conversation.\nThe lesson is not to copy famous artists blindly. The lesson is to keep the bio connected to the\njourney and the current campaign."
