    "source": "Social Media Optimization",
    "page": 6,
    "text": "Social Media Optimization\nProfile Photo\nRecognizable, creative, and consistent across platforms\nA profile photo is not just decoration. It is the smallest version of your artist brand. It appears in\ncomments, stories, messages, searches, feeds, playlist shares, and fan screenshots. If it is\nblurry, random, corporate, or hard to read, it weakens the first impression.\nYou may not yet have massive HPEs, major PR, or a large marketing team pushing people to\nyour page. That means the simple parts matter more: profile photo, bio, highlights, grid, reels,\nand the first few posts people see.\nPractical Rule\nUse professional creative headshots, album artwork, or release-related profile images. Avoid passport-style\nphotos, corporate headshots, and random low-quality selfies."
