    "source": "Social Media Optimization",
    "page": 11,
    "text": "Social Media Optimization\nPosting With Purpose\nStop treating the grid like a junk drawer\nStop Posting Randomly\nDo not post only because you forgot to post for two days. Plan your posts, create purpose, curate the look,\nand schedule when possible.\nUse A Laptop Or Desktop\nMobile is convenient, but desktop view helps you see your page more broadly and catch issues you may miss\non your phone.\nGrid vs. Reels\nInstagram separates the profile grid and Reels page. Both should be curated. Replace bad Reel covers and\navoid letting poor thumbnails damage the grid.\nUse Instagram scheduling and Meta tools when helpful. The point is not to become robotic. The\npoint is to stop letting random posting damage the customer journey."
